# Keep binary assets byte-exact.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is common on Windows checkouts. Git auto-detects binary
# files by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8000 bytes, but a ReportLab PDF
# begins with a plain-text header and its first NUL falls past that window, so
# Git misreads the recruiting resumes as text and rewrites LF -> CRLF on
# checkout, corrupting them. Mark binaries explicitly.
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.svg -text
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
